  "tagline": "A traditional Persian dance mastered by the performer Jamileh.",
  "insight": "Qasemabadi is recognized as a traditional Persian dance, notably performed by the Iranian dancer and actress Jamileh during her career in the 20th century.",
  "profile": "Qasemabadi is a traditional Persian dance. It is identified as a dance form in which the Iranian performer Jamileh was considered a master. The dance is categorized alongside other Persian dance styles such as Bandari and classical Persian dances.",
  "profile_long": "Qasemabadi is a traditional Persian dance documented in the context of 20th-century Iranian popular entertainment. The dance is recognized as one of the styles mastered by the Iranian actress and dancer Jamileh (Fatemeh Sadeghi), who was a prominent figure in Iranian cabaret and cinema during the 1960s and 1970s. Jamileh, who was born in 1946 in Tehran, became a master of several Persian dance forms, including Qasemabadi, Bandari, and various classical Persian dances. Her career, which spanned from her early life in the siâh theater scene to her later performances in Los Angeles, helped popularize these dance styles through her film roles and cabaret appearances. Beyond its association with Jamileh's repertoire, the specific technical, cultural, and historical details of the Qasemabadi dance are not described in the sources.",
